record legeos.decision.homegarden-activity-grown-places/1 : decision {
    title "Homegarden: Home is a field of Places grown from the user's own actions, aged in session time, positioned by memory"
    state superseded
    scope [
        path "crates/lege-field/**",
        path "crates/lege-session-core/**",
        path "interfaces/dbus/org.legeos.HomeGarden1.xml",
        path "services/lege-sessiond/**",
        path "shell/lege-shell/**"
    ]
    topic homegarden
    decision """
        Home deals with the user's stuff; the bar deals with the machine. Directories appear on Home as Folder tiles (Places) because the user opened, launched into, edited under or returned to them; they grow when activity concentrates there, hold their place while used, shrink and finally leave when neglected, and regrow where they were. A tile may change size, appear or disappear because of the user's aggregated actions on its path; it may never change position because of them; and it may never move, shrink or displace a tile the user placed, moved, resized or pinned. Tending happens only at tending moments (Home reveal, session start, an explicit garden.tend) and never while the user is looking. The tender emits Place, Resize and Remove only, every op with a reason, applied as one undoable batch. Time is Garden time: sessions counted and unlocked-session runtime accumulated at session start/unlock/lock/sleep/logout edges, never wall-clock; a machine that is off ages nothing. Relevance is evidence x recency-in-garden-time x breadth: a place used across several sessions with several roles outranks one burst of saves; machine churn (build output, caches, hidden dirs) never counts. Content changes may alter what an already-earned Place shows but never create one. Every visual variable has one job: shape = mode, material = identity, colour = state, size = relevance, position = memory. No context is ever turned into a Project by the system; no group is ever inferred.
        """
    context """
        docs/garden/garden.md (the user's correction: no assumed main project, no fabricated first boot, no widgets that could be menus, closer integration with the file system, an organic system that notices where you work and tends it), docs/garden/homegarden-activity-grown-home.md (the model), docs/garden/garden2.md (session time instead of days, growth forms, branches vs blooms). @legeos.assessment.home-vision-review-20260905 left the mostly-empty cold Home unresolved; this is the answer: the emptiness is read, not filled.
        """
    consequences """
        Revises the consequences of @legeos.decision.home-field-stable-bounded-semantic-grammar: 'content-driven' means index/content events; user-action-driven size change at tending moments is admitted. Supersedes the 'repack on activity' clause of @legeos.work.home-developer-setup-preview with 'resize in place at tending moments'. Phases 0-3 (ledger, Garden Clock, planner, tending at reveal, rung-aware Folder tile with roles row and branch body) are built first; growth forms/facets, blooms, material identity, sibling groups and a Wide-vs-Tall geometry axis are deferred until Phase 4 (a day's hands-on) judges the model. Wall-clock never appears in the garden's ageing; the Garden Clock needs session edges from Lifecycle1.
        """
    derived_from [
        @legeos.decision.home-field-stable-bounded-semantic-grammar,
        @legeos.decision.home-is-momentary-and-placeable-objects-are-containers,
        @legeos.decision.representation-ladder-is-the-organizing-principle
    ]
    implements [ @legeos.constraint.services-not-indicators ]
    supported_by [ @legeos.evidence.homegarden-phases-0-3-tests-20260908/1 ]
    source {
        kind external
        role origin
        document "garden-design-conversation-20260907"
        use """
            the philosophy: activity earns space, roles not applications, zero-polling decay, spatial persistence, three visibility states
            """
    }
    source {
        kind external
        role rationale
        document "garden2-growth-forms-and-session-time-20260907"
        use """
            session time replaces days; shape/material/colour/size/position each have one job; branches vs blooms
            """
    }
    source {
        kind internal
        role origin
        document "homegarden-plan-20260907"
        use """
            the model, the ledger, the planner rules and the phases
            """
    }
}

